{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1772832344163,"sessionID":"ses_33af55a7bffeFJoqGAyOhXBen3","part":{"id":"prt_cc50ac855001eQT8MfZPaTx6Xw","sessionID":"ses_33af55a7bffeFJoqGAyOhXBen3","messageID":"msg_cc50aa66a001P3iHmm2blVHYoN","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_bgcw974y1a8t_1","tool":"glob","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"**/test*/**/*.md"},"output":"No files found","title":"","metadata":{"count":0,"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1772832344153,"end":1772832344162}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The user wants me to write a comprehensive test specification document based on the feature plan they've provided. They explicitly state I should NOT write actual test code, but rather write in plain language focusing on \"what should happen\" not \"how to test it\".\n\nLet me analyze the feature plan and create a thorough test specification covering:\n\n1. Behaviors That MUST Be Verified - each behavior from the plan with success criteria\n2. Edge Cases - empty/null inputs, boundary conditions, invalid states, concurrent operations, error conditions\n3. What Constitutes Failure - criteria for test failure, error messages expected, rollback behavior\n4. Out of Scope - explicitly list what NOT to test\n\nI need to output a JSON object representing the Write tool call with the filePath and content.\n\nLet me think about the directory structure - where should this test spec be written? Looking at the feature, it involves:\n- pipeline/server_client.py\n- pipeline/tui.py\n- server/hub.go\n- server/api.go\n- server/templates/client.html\n\nSince this is a test specification, I should look at where test specs are typically stored in this project. Let me first explore the project structure to understand where to place this file.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":"850b53dca0cd77ffb4bc6dcc7a2edbd2b512f7b4c808726aab15ea7a0ac34550"}]}}}}
